  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "Evidence: The jump from singleprofile (config_005, acc=0.532) to multiprofile with avgpool (config_031, acc=0.715) shows that profile aggregation is the dominant design lever, yielding ~18 points. The aggregation mechanism itself (avgpool) is a simple mean; a transformer aggregator can model inter-profile dependencies and may capture complementary information across profiles that avgpool discards. Question: Does transformer aggregation outperform avgpool when all other components (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, concat fusion, multiprofile) are held constant at the current best? This is a clean single-variable test of the highest-impact design choice. Rationale: With 7 experiments remaining, exploiting the strongest evidence (multiprofile + aggregation) by upgrading the aggregation to a more expressive mechanism is the best expected-value move. If transformer helps, it sets a new ceiling; if it doesn't, we've confirmed avgpool is sufficient and can pivot to fusion or encoder choices. Expected cost: transformer aggregation adds self-attention over profiles, so I estimate ~5.5–6.5 GPU hours (moderately higher than config_031's 4.49), which is affordable within the remaining budget and justified by the potential accuracy gain."
}

